    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. But the part about \"unaided memory\" is what's tripping me up. It feels a bit vague. Like, if I develop a really specific optimization pattern while working on their private database, and then I use that same pattern a month later for a different client, can they actually sue me if they prove I \"remembered\" it? Where's the line between my own skill and their confidential info?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
